# The fields the checks read from documents that no tool decodes: a HelmRelease and the sources it
# names, as scripts/render reads them; a FluxInstance, as scripts/pod-security-check reads it; and a
# Kustomization of an application that applies from a GitRepository or an OCIRepository, that
# source, and the source object operator-definitions.yaml names, as scripts/kubernetes-validate
# reads them. Each reads them with jq, by exact name, and hands a tool only what it derives from
# them: helm a chart's URL, name and version as arguments and values files it writes, kustomize a
# kustomization it writes from a release's post-renderers or the instance's patches, curl the URL of
# a repository's archive at a tag, tar the directories to unpack, and kustomize a directory of what
# it unpacked.
#
# roots: HelmRelease OCIRepository HelmRepository FluxInstance GitRepository Kustomization
#
# The API server drops a field of a custom resource that its schema does not name, by exact name,
# so the cluster ignores a key that only differs from one of these by case, as the checks would;
# the checks refuse such a key rather than skip it: one that encoding/json's folding matches to a
# field of the list (ASCII letters without regard to case, U+017F as s and U+212A as k). A type
# marked open holds other fields as well, which the checks do not read; every other type is all a
# tool is handed at that position, and any other key there is refused. One field a line, as in
# kustomization-fields; TYPE * open marks a type as open.
HelmRelease * open
HelmRelease apiVersion value
HelmRelease kind value
HelmRelease metadata Metadata
HelmRelease spec HelmReleaseSpec
Metadata * open
Metadata name value
Metadata namespace value
